# Right model for the job (quality first, cost second)
- **Highest-capability model** → architecture/planning, ALL financial/accounting work, code-review + financial-agent passes, migration authoring, adversarial verification, any ambiguous/high-stakes call.
- **Mid-tier** → routine feature code, UI wiring, non-financial backend, tests.
- **Fast/cheap** → mechanical edits, formatting, docs, bulk inventory/search passes.
Escalate to a higher tier the instant a task touches money, schema, RLS, migrations, or the linkage law. When in doubt, escalate — a wrong financial change dwarfs any model cost.
